   "title": "START HERE",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "START HERE - JOY-LTX 2.5 MULTISHOT (one story, several shots, one video)\n\nThe writer turns your premise into N shot prompts; the sampler renders each shot with the two-pass pipeline and JOINS them:\n- continue = the previous shot's last frames AND sound are pinned into the next one -> one seamless take of any length (writer join style \"extend take\").\n- cut = only the sound is pinned: the voice carries across a picture cut, the picture follows the new shot prompt (writer \"cuts\" / \"continuous scene with cuts\").\n- fresh = independent shots.\nSame people in every shot: identity_ref (on the sampler) attaches a frame of shot 1 to the later shots - no reference photos needed. identity_strength 0.3-0.6 keeps the people and lets the framing move; 1.0 copies the framing too.\n\n1. SCENE IDEA. 2. Writer: num_shots = how many shots (and a model you have). 3. MASTER CONTROLS: render size + seconds PER SHOT + upscale (auto; x2/x1.5/none by hand if you accept streaming). 4. Writer join style to match the join. 5. USE I2V (optional): first frame of shot 1. 6. Run.\n\nVRAM = one shot; take length = shots x seconds. Fewer, longer shots = fewer joins (24 GB: 4 x 30 s single pass works). Read-me note: models + links."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
